Fix an integer $1\le s \le M/2$ and a constant $c_0>0$.

(i) Let Assumption 1 be satisfied. Then Assumptions \RE s{c_0} and \REm ss{c_0} hold with $\kappa (s,c_0) =\kappa (s,s,c_0)=\kappa_1 (s,c_0)$. Moreover, for any subset $J_0$ of $\{1,\dots,M\}$ with cardinality $|J_0|\le s$, and any $\bD\in \RR^M$ such that \begin{equation} |\bD_{J_0^c}|_1 \le c_0 |\bD_{J_0}|_1 \end{equation} we have \begin{equation*} \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}|P_{01} X \bD|_2 \ge  \kappa_1 (s,c_0) |\bD_{J_{01}}|_2 \end{equation*} where $P_{01}$ is the projector in $\RR^M$ on the linear span of the columns of $X_{J_{01}}$.

(ii) Let Assumption 2 be satisfied. Then Assumptions \RE s{c_0} and \REm sm{c_0} hold with $\kappa (s,c_0) =\kappa (s,m,c_0)=\kappa_2 (s,m,c_0)$. Moreover, for any subset $J_0$ of $\{1,\dots,M\}$ with cardinality $|J_0|\le s$, and any $\bD\in \RR^M$ such that (\ref{l21}) holds we have \begin{equation*} \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}|P_{01} X \bD|_2 \ge  \kappa_2 (s,m,c_0) |\bD_{J_{01}}|_2. \end{equation*}

